ideaSummary:
Brave Sports & Enterprise Academy (BSEA) is a skills development and talent discovery program that combines sports training with enterprise education to tackle youth unemployment and underutilized sports potential in Edo State.

The Academy will identify and train grassroots sports talents through a Community Talent League (CTL), offer industry-relevant certifications (in coaching, refereeing, fitness training, and sports event management), and equip young people with entrepreneurial skills related to the sports and wellness industry.

This initiative responds directly to the widening gap in Edo State where youth talents in sports remain untapped, and career opportunities in the sports industry are misunderstood or inaccessible. Through strategic mentorship and partnerships with local sports associations, schools, and community leaders, BSEA will:

Host local sports talent discovery leagues across LGAs;

Train youths in event coordination and management, building capacity for future tournaments and entertainment events;

Facilitate certified training in coaching, fitness instruction, officiating, and digital content creation for sports;

Organize mentorship sessions with professionals in sports business, marketing, and wellness coaching.
Our goal is to build a sustainable talent pipeline while enabling sports to become a career path and business opportunity for Edo youths.

